The usage text hid nine of the fourteen commands
=================================================

`--search`, `--prompt-block`, `--memory`, `--remember`, `--recall`, `--scope`, `--voice`, `--say` and
`--transcript` are all accepted by the argument parser and all absent from `quixi`'s own usage output.
A command that works but does not appear is a command nobody finds, and the memory and voice commands
are the entire reason this edition exists.

Grouped by what they cost: prompts, inspection that costs no model call, memory, and voice — with the
real arity for each, taken from the handlers rather than guessed. `--remember` takes wing, room and name
and reads the content from stdin; `--recall` takes `--limit`; `--say` takes `--dry-run`; `--scope` and
`--transcript` take no arguments at all.

